<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n34815" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνᾰλύω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλύω ἐν</span>
			, <i>revel in, exult over</i>, c. dat., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. καὶ ἐνυβρίζειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					2.369
				</span></i>
			, cf.<i><span class="en">
				372
			</span></i>; simply, <i>dwell upon</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅταν ἐναλύῃ αὐτοῖς ὁ λόγος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philostr.
					<u>Im.</u>
					2.8
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεραπείᾳ τῇ περὶ τὴν θεὸν
			ἐ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Hld.
				7.9
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κόμη ἐναλύουσα τῷ
			μετώπῳ</span> hair <i>hanging wildly over</i> the face, <i><span class="en">
				Philostr.
				<u>Im.</u>
				1.10
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
